<h2>Check your containers</h2>
<p>Run this next to your <code>docker-compose.yml</code>:</p>
<pre><code>docker compose ps</code></pre>
<p>
  A healthy install shows three services running: <code>openinflowwww-relay</code> (127.0.0.1:8787),
  <code>openinflowwww-app</code> (127.0.0.1:3001) and <code>openinflowwww-autoheal</code>, which restarts unhealthy
  services. <code>openinflowwww-tunnel</code> shows up only if you started the <code>tunnel</code> profile.
</p>

<h2>Check the relay</h2>
<p>The relay's liveness probe needs no token. It is what the Docker healthcheck calls:</p>
<pre><code>curl http://127.0.0.1:8787/livez
# {"ok":true}</code></pre>
<p>
  If a service keeps restarting, <code>docker compose logs openinflowwww-relay</code> (or <code>openinflowwww-app</code>)
  shows why. If the logs don't help, <a href="{{ site.repo }}/issues/new">open an issue</a> with them.
</p>
